# A VS match settled after "Go!": Pikachu (P1) vs Peach (P2) on Onett, no input
# on either side, so both fighters stand at their spawn points and the camera
# frames the same thing on both sides.
#
# Dolphin cannot be booted straight into a match -- the Gecko and [OnFrame]
# boot-to-mode patches both leave it on the Main Menu, and Final Destination
# is locked in the test save -- so the route is the real one: Main Menu ->
# VS. Mode -> Melee -> character select (P1 hand to Pikachu, P2 hand to Peach,
# each with its own controller) -> Start -> stage select -> Onett. The hand
# moves ~7.5 px per frame at full deflection; the timings below were found
# by capture and are what they are.
#
# The port boots into the same lineup through the debug-VS scene; it runs
# the default 2:00 time match now so the timer is on screen on both sides.
description: VS match settled, Pikachu vs Peach on Onett
run_frames: 360
ref_frames: 2400
align: search
window: 8
# Measured: the port shows "Go!" at frame ~100, Dolphin at dump ~1630.
ref_lead: -1530
env: MELEE_BOOT_MODE=14
env: MELEE_BOOT_MATCH=13,12,9,0,0
ref_input: 236:+START
ref_input: 240:-START
ref_input: 400:+START
ref_input: 404:-START
ref_input: 760:MAIN:0.5:0.0
ref_input: 768:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 820:+A
ref_input: 824:-A
ref_input: 950:+A
ref_input: 954:-A
ref_input: 1000:P2:+A
ref_input: 1004:P2:-A
ref_input: 1060:MAIN:0.5:1.0
ref_input: 1120:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1130:MAIN:1.0:0.5
ref_input: 1140:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1150:MAIN:0.5:0.0
ref_input: 1157:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1170:+A
ref_input: 1174:-A
ref_input: 1180:P2:MAIN:0.5:1.0
ref_input: 1240:P2:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1250:P2:MAIN:1.0:0.5
ref_input: 1260:P2:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1270:P2:MAIN:0.5:0.0
ref_input: 1277:P2:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1290:P2:+A
ref_input: 1294:P2:-A
ref_input: 1340:+START
ref_input: 1344:-START
ref_input: 1420:MAIN:0.5:1.0
ref_input: 1452:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1480:+A
ref_input: 1484:-A
checks: 250, 320
